Refactor the code below to resolve the SonarQube issue described here.

## Issue
Rule: dart:S3776 (Cognitive Complexity of functions should not be too high)
Message: Refactor this method to reduce its Cognitive Complexity from 16 to the 15 allowed.
File: lib/features/auth/presentation/login_page.dart
Flagged lines: 81 (the code below covers lines 80-192)

## Rule description
Cognitive Complexity measures how hard a function's control flow is to
understand. Each break in linear flow (if, else, ternary, loop, catch,
switch, logical-operator sequence) adds to the score, and nesting adds more.
Reduce it by extracting nested parts into well-named private methods or
widgets, using early returns, and flattening nested conditionals, while
keeping behavior unchanged.

## Context
Examples of the same kind of refactoring, from other code:

Example 1: Flatten nested conditionals with early returns
Before:
```dart
String status(Order o) {
  if (o.paid) {
    if (o.shipped) {
      if (o.delivered) {
        return 'Delivered';
      } else {
        return 'In transit';
      }
    } else {
      return 'Awaiting shipment';
    }
  } else {
    return 'Unpaid';
  }
}
```
After:
```dart
String status(Order o) {
  if (!o.paid) return 'Unpaid';
  if (!o.shipped) return 'Awaiting shipment';
  return o.delivered ? 'Delivered' : 'In transit';
}
```

Example 2: Extract part of a large build method into a helper
Before:
```dart
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return Column(
    children: [
      if (items.isEmpty)
        const Text('Empty')
      else
        for (final item in items)
          item.isDone
              ? ListTile(title: Text(item.name), trailing: const Icon(Icons.check))
              : ListTile(title: Text(item.name)),
      if (isLoading) const CircularProgressIndicator() else const SizedBox(),
    ],
  );
}
```
After:
```dart
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return Column(
    children: [
      ..._buildItems(),
      if (isLoading) const CircularProgressIndicator() else const SizedBox(),
    ],
  );
}

List<Widget> _buildItems() {
  if (items.isEmpty) return const [Text('Empty')];
  return [for (final item in items) _buildItem(item)];
}

Widget _buildItem(Item item) {
  return ListTile(
    title: Text(item.name),
    trailing: item.isDone ? const Icon(Icons.check) : null,
  );
}
```

